---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ImageToolGrid from '../components/ImageToolGrid.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Free Online Image Tools — Resize, Compress, Crop & More | ConvertAnyFile" description="Free browser-based image tools with no source-image upload. Resize, compress, crop, rotate, inspect metadata, bulk rename images, and remove visible watermarks locally.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="site-container hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Image Tools</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Free Online Image Tools</span><h1>Private image tools that run in your browser.</h1><p>Resize, compress, crop, rotate, inspect metadata, bulk rename image files, or use focused watermark-removal workflows. Working tools keep source-image processing in the browser instead of sending files to a remote conversion queue.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Utility platform preview</span><h2>Six everyday image workflows now share one browser-first foundation.</h2><p><a href="/resize-image/"><strong>Resize</strong></a>, <a href="/compress-image/"><strong>Compress</strong></a>, <a href="/crop-image/"><strong>Crop</strong></a>, and <a href="/rotate-image/"><strong>Rotate / Flip</strong></a> reuse the same ImageMagick WebAssembly worker. <a href="/image-metadata/"><strong>Image Metadata</strong></a> adds local inspection and cleaning, while <a href="/bulk-rename-images/"><strong>Bulk Rename</strong></a> changes filenames without re-encoding image bytes.</p></div><ImageToolGrid /></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Shared batch behavior</span><h2>One predictable workflow across utility transforms.</h2><p>Resize, Compress, Crop, and Rotate / Flip share file admission, 200 MB batch safety limits, duplicate detection, clear skip feedback, cancel behavior, retry for failed files, per-file downloads, and ZIP packaging. Settings changes invalidate old outputs instead of leaving stale downloads on screen.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Local by design</strong><p>Supported transforms decode, process and encode images in the browser. Bulk Rename does not transform pixels at all. Metadata viewing stays local; metadata cleaning creates a newly encoded copy and says so explicitly.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Choose the right tool</span><h2>Start with the change you actually need.</h2></div><div class="comparison-table-wrap"><table class="comparison-table"><thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Best when</th><th>Main controls</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td><a href="/resize-image/"><strong>Resize Image</strong></a></td><td>You need smaller, larger, proportional, or exact image dimensions.</td><td>Target box, exact size, percentage, presets</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/compress-image/"><strong>Compress Image</strong></a></td><td>You need a smaller file while balancing visual quality.</td><td>Quality, Same/JPG/WebP/PNG, size comparison</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/crop-image/"><strong>Crop Image</strong></a></td><td>You need a centered social, landscape, portrait, or exact crop.</td><td>1:1, 4:3, 3:2, 16:9, 9:16, exact center size</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/rotate-image/"><strong>Rotate / Flip</strong></a></td><td>A batch shares an orientation or mirroring problem.</td><td>90/180/270°, horizontal flip, vertical flip</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/image-metadata/"><strong>Image Metadata</strong></a></td><td>You want to inspect detected profiles/attributes or make a cleaned copy.</td><td>Metadata viewer, preserve color profile, cleaner</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/bulk-rename-images/"><strong>Bulk Rename Images</strong></a></td><td>You want consistent filenames without changing image bytes.</td><td>{'{name}'}, {'{n}'}, padding, lowercase</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/gemini-ai-logo-remover/"><strong>Gemini Watermark Remover</strong></a></td><td>A small visible Gemini-style sparkle watermark or similar compact corner mark.</td><td>Circle, 4-Point Star</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/remove-watermark/"><strong>Remove Watermark</strong></a></td><td>The visible mark can be rectangular, round, diamond-shaped, sparkle-shaped or text.</td><td>Rectangle, Circle, Square, Diamond, Star, Text</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Roadmap discipline</span><h2>Interactive or higher-risk tools stay planned until their behavior is validated.</h2><p>Background utilities, blur, larger object removal, and automatic background removal remain roadmap items. Interactive free-position crop handles are also intentionally separate from the current deterministic centered-crop preview.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Shared engine where it fits</strong><p>Deterministic transforms reuse the image worker. Stateful visual repair keeps the mask editor. Filename-only operations skip image re-encoding. Each tool uses the smallest processing path that fits the job.</p></div></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
